    text: "---"
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "scene 005.2 — the mountain obelisks"
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "scene meta:"
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "location: Island mountain peak / slope"
  - line: 21
    type: narration
    text: "time: year 47"
  - line: 22
    type: narration
    text: "participants: Mountain Giants, Nephoretti"
  - line: 23
    type: narration
    text: "focus: Mountain Giants carve the first 30ft singing granite obelisk, discovering that geometric proportions amplify vrill-resonance and consciousness-touch."
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "continuity: Takes place 32 years after the first pyramid collapse in scene 005.1"
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "presentation: undecided"
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "The mountain Giants' obelisk project succeeded where the pyramid had failed—partially because vertical structures had simpler stress-dynamics, but mostly because charcoal-grey Giants possessed an instinctive understanding of how stone wanted to stand."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "The first successful obelisk rose thirty feet from a mountain slope overlooking the beaches—a single piece of granite shaped through consciousness-touch rather than carved or stacked."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "The mountain Giants had learned to ask the stone what shape it preferred, then help it remember that preference through patient communion."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "The result was a pillar that sang when wind passed through microscopic channels within its structure."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "Not music exactly."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "More like sustained harmonic that made other stones nearby vibrate in sympathy."
  - line: 35
    type: narration
    text: "Nephoretti discovered that standing near the obelisk while practicing vrill-manipulation made their consciousness-touch more precise, more responsive."
  - line: 36
    type: narration
    text: "The geometry itself seemed to focus intention, amplifying what was already present without adding external power."
  - line: 38
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "\"Accidental discovery,\""
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "the lead mountain Giant rumbled—they had learned basic spoken language now, though their deep voices made every word sound like distant thunder. \"Built for beauty. Found utility.\""
  - line: 41
    type: narration
    text: "More obelisks followed."
  - line: 42
    type: narration
    text: "Different sizes, different proportions, different harmonic frequencies."
  - line: 43
    type: narration
    text: "Some stood alone on prominent peaks."
  - line: 44
    type: narration
    text: "Others clustered in groups of three or five, creating interference patterns that the Nephoretti were still trying to understand."
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "A few failed catastrophically—stone cracking under its own weight or shattering when underground water expanded during freeze-thaw cycles."
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "But enough succeeded to transform the island's silhouette."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "Where once only natural mountain had dominated, now stone spires rose like fingers pointing at sky, each singing its own frequency, all contributing to a harmony that made the entire island feel more alive, more resonant."
  - line: 50
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "year 93"

